From a2ea8f2044a5f9a23181ceb246afededc6ab5be4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the simplified rounding under the GUI, where
 the caller asks for it

On an integrated Radeon the frames of a profile 5 picture with the player
information open still take more than a 41.7 ms film refresh after pass 3
writes what pass 8 takes of the picture under each pixel: converting a pixel
drawn over back to codes takes PQ round trips that the affine profiles do not.
The frames of profile 7 FEL and 8.1 with the same GUI fit.

dvbridge_render_simplify_gui() lets the caller ask, frame by frame, for passes
3 and 8 without the correction of the first form of drawn_over(), the float
error of the round trip of the picture under the pixel. Pass 3 (PICTURE_FLAG)
writes only whether that form holds, into a target of its own of a byte a
pixel; pass 8 (PAIRS_SIMPLE) converts the even pixel's luma and the pair's
chroma from one call. A pixel drawn over can come out one code apart from the
exact conversion; nothing else changes: the pixels nothing is drawn over, the
frames without anything drawn over them and the affine profiles (7, 8) are
never drawn by these programs, and with it not asked for every program and
every byte is that of before.

Fail-closed: both programs or neither (said once in the log), and where the
target of the flags cannot be made, the exact corrections; the rounding is then
the exact one whatever is asked. dvbridge_render_gui_simplifiable() says
whether a frame's picture can be drawn that way, and
dvbridge_render_gui_simplified() whether the last frame was.

Measured with the software bridge on 162 frames of three profile 5, two FEL
and one 8.1 picture under nine kinds of GUI, and with PQ subtitles:
- not asked for: the same bytes as before on lavapipe, and on an integrated
  Radeon and an RTX 4080 through D3D12; the GLSL of the 13 programs of before,
  the same text;
- asked for: in the 81 profile 5 frames, 3,455,489 (lavapipe), 2,118,564
  (Radeon) and 2,046,906 (RTX 4080) codes changed of about 650 million pixels
  drawn over, none by more than one code, none outside the pixels drawn over;
  no frame of profile 7 or 8.1 changed;
- six mutations of the two programs make that check fail; either program not
  compiling, or either target not made, leaves every byte as before;
- GPU time of a frame on the Radeon through D3D12 (radeonsi not measured), the
  player information over profile 5: 46.8 to 48.0 ms exact, 35.0 to 35.1 ms
  simplified; a window over a dimmed screen: 57.0 to 58.5 ms, 42.0 to 42.4 ms;
  FEL and 8.1, unchanged.
